{
  "findings": [
    {
      "title": "[P2] Preserve the global claim inbox during workspace switches",
      "body": "Every workspace connection calls `clearDataStores()`, so this clears the global `incomingClaims` and `outgoingClaims` arrays as well as workspace-specific state. The inbox loaders in `MainPanel` and `IdentityLinksView` only rerun when the user or component changes, not when the workspace changes, so switching workspaces makes the badge and claims tab remain empty until a remount or reload.",
      "confidence_score": 0.98,
      "priority": 2,
      "code_location": {
        "absolute_file_path": "/home/codex/projects/family-tree/frontend/src/hooks/useWorkspaceStore.ts",
        "line_range": {
          "start": 122,
          "end": 122
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "title": "[P2] Allow proposers to cancel after losing workspace access",
      "body": "When an editor creates a claim and their workspace access is later revoked, the claim remains in their global outgoing inbox but this dependency rejects the cancellation before `cancel_claim` can verify that they are the proposer. The resulting Cancel button always fails with 403, leaving the user's own pending proposal active until the recipient acts or it expires.",
      "confidence_score": 0.93,
      "priority": 2,
      "code_location": {
        "absolute_file_path": "/home/codex/projects/family-tree/backend/app/api/routes/identity_link_claims.py",
        "line_range": {
          "start": 130,
          "end": 130
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "title": "[P2] Prevent editors from rewriting another proposer's claim",
      "body": "If two editors can write the source member and are both friends with the same target, the second editor finds the first editor's pending claim here and overwrites its note and expiry. Because `proposed_by` remains unchanged, the target then sees modified text attributed to the original proposer; only claims created by the current actor should be refreshed, or this case should be rejected.",
      "confidence_score": 0.97,
      "priority": 2,
      "code_location": {
        "absolute_file_path": "/home/codex/projects/family-tree/backend/app/services/identity_link_claims.py",
        "line_range": {
          "start": 136,
          "end": 140
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "title": "[P2] Enforce pending-claim uniqueness atomically",
      "body": "With two simultaneous proposals for the same source member and target user, both transactions can observe no pending row and insert separate claims because the migration adds no matching unique or partial-unique constraint. This produces duplicate inbox entries and notifications and allows the copies to be completed independently; the deduplication must be enforced in PostgreSQL and its conflict handled.",
      "confidence_score": 0.96,
      "priority": 2,
      "code_location": {
        "absolute_file_path": "/home/codex/projects/family-tree/backend/app/services/identity_link_claims.py",
        "line_range": {
          "start": 126,
          "end": 131
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "title": "[P2] Notify the proposer when a claim is declined",
      "body": "When the recipient declines a claim, this block only commits the state change and never enqueues the new `identity_link_claim_decided` notification. Unlike completion, the proposer receives neither a durable notification nor an SSE event and cannot learn the outcome until manually reloading the outgoing inbox.",
      "confidence_score": 0.98,
      "priority": 2,
      "code_location": {
        "absolute_file_path": "/home/codex/projects/family-tree/backend/app/services/identity_link_claims.py",
        "line_range": {
          "start": 244,
          "end": 246
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "title": "[P2] Notify the source owner when editor approval is pending",
      "body": "When an editor proposed the claim, `source_approved_by` is null, so completion creates a link that remains `proposed` pending the source owner's approval. This branch only sends owner notifications when the link is already verified, leaving the source owner with no `identity_link_proposed` notification that review is required.",
      "confidence_score": 0.97,
      "priority": 2,
      "code_location": {
        "absolute_file_path": "/home/codex/projects/family-tree/backend/app/services/identity_link_claims.py",
        "line_range": {
          "start": 371,
          "end": 372
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "title": "[P2] Route member search through a store action",
      "body": "This component calls `WorkspaceService` directly, bypassing the Zustand action layer and making loading, cancellation, and test behavior local to the dialog. The repository requires components to only read store state and call store actions ([AGENTS.md:51-59](/home/codex/projects/family-tree/AGENTS.md#L51-L59)); expose this search through the appropriate store as the other member searches do.",
      "confidence_score": 0.99,
      "priority": 2,
      "code_location": {
        "absolute_file_path": "/home/codex/projects/family-tree/frontend/src/components/view/identity-links-view/CompleteIdentityLinkClaimDialog.tsx",
        "line_range": {
          "start": 67,
          "end": 69
        }
      }
    }
  ],
  "overall_correctness": "patch is incorrect",
  "overall_explanation": "The new claim flow has authorization, concurrency, notification, and state-lifecycle defects that can leave claims duplicated, silently pending, or impossible to cancel. It also bypasses the repository's required frontend data-flow architecture.",
  "overall_confidence_score": 0.97
}
